#: ../../source/docs/common-thecubeorange-overview.rst:14
#: 1b22957b897041278100be3621a90b9e
msgid "The Cube Orange autopilot is the latest and most powerful model in the CubePilot ecosystem. Designed for hobby users, commercial system integrators and UAS manufacturers the Cube Orange autopilot is part of a wide ecosystem of autopilot modules and carrier boards. All Cube models are compatible with all carriers which allows users to choose an off the shelf carrier board that best suits their needs. System designers are able to integrate the Cube directly into their designs via published carrier board specifications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-thecubeorange-overview.rst:16
#: b6e7e6153a3e4f17bc7b9d94d332190f
msgid "The Cube Orange is available as a standalone module or as a package with a new updated version of the original carrier board that now includes an integrated ADS-B In module from uAvionics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-thecubeorange-overview.rst:19
#: 9954dcfa8e4142128bb038b91f5c0fe3
msgid "ADS-B Carrier Board"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-thecubeorange-overview.rst:21
#: 39627c81d1f242e395530483442c8030
msgid "The new ADS-B carrier boards overall footprint is identical to the standard versions and the main changes compared to the original carrier are as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-thecubeorange-overview.rst:23
#: 505642106e98479bbc78c9dee10be894
msgid "Integration of uAvonix ADS-B IN Receiver on Serial 5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-thecubeorange-overview.rst:24
#: 28832fbde12b4182bf9f1a0ce9421ac4
msgid "Built-In ADS-B Antenna"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-thecubeorange-overview.rst:25
#: 81195e57272a4378a2c2dc0cebee589d
msgid "Removal of Intel Edison Bay and Debug USB Ports"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-thecubeorange-overview.rst:27
#: f46409d6f3a64e739da094e58764f793
msgid "All other specification and external connections remain identical to the original board as listed on the Cube Black page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-thecubeorange-overview.rst:30
#: 4f8e3a42826f4c9f9cdfedc008f26123
msgid "Cube Orange/+ Features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-thecubeorange-overview.rst:32
#: 685e0bf5c1a14936a7fe807bfae66c55
msgid "Faster H7 SOC with 1MB ram"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-thecubeorange-overview.rst:33
#: 06107f95c9684b4da3f8d0ad94895c90
msgid "Upgraded triple redundant IMU sensors for extra redundancy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-thecubeorange-overview.rst:34
#: 1cb28d2151404a51964ce27c51302c8d
msgid "2 sets of IMU are vibration-isolated mechanically, reducing the effect of frame vibration to state estimation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-thecubeorange-overview.rst:35
#: db99ee2d3bc24ab1b45ecf05d458fa37
msgid "IMUs are temperature-controlled by onboard heating resistors, allowing optimum working temperature of IMUs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-thecubeorange-overview.rst:36
#: 80de9aad41a941f19079ede4847e1d92
msgid "The entire flight management unit(FMU) and inertial management unit(IMU) are housed in a reatively small form factor (a cube)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-thecubeorange-overview.rst:37
#: e9f685e1a41c4fef9c6954139ad2496c
msgid "Fully CubePilot carrierboard compatible, all inputs and outputs go through a 80-pin DF17 connector, allowing a plug-in solution for manufacturers of commercial systems. Manufacturers can design their own carrier boards to suit their specific needs now and in the future."
msgstr ""

